{"1762697756076839193":{"a":"<p>Cleaned and put a new coat of varnish on the old @ClubCyberiaIndy founders plaque. It got a little scuffed when we packed up shop. t.co</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762697756076839193\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762697756076839193</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1762697756076839193</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762697756076839193\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-28T04:34:29Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1762814127590834494":{"a":"<p>Is Experience better than using the correct tools? Or can an experienced person make a good box using junk tools? My makerspace experience totally agrees with this, in general. Good tools enable inexperienced people to do amazing work.<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vk_3BBx3Uak\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/vk_3BBx3Uak\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\"></iframe><p class=\"embed-fallback\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vk_3BBx3Uak\">Watch on YouTube</a></p></div>","m":"<h1>Post 1762814127590834494</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762814127590834494\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-28T12:16:54Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1762820482988957839":{"a":"<p>A friend brought me a Coleco Adam, Console with Adam expansion, and Atari 2600 expansion. Lots of spare parts and memory upgrades. Going on the desk with the Commodore 64, DECTalk DCT-1, Sony PS2, and Nabu PC. I think there&#x27;s a bad video memory chip and a 7400 series TTL chip. 😃 t.co</p>\n<blockquote class=\"twitter-tweet embed embed-tweet\"><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762820482988957839\">https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762820482988957839</a></blockquote>","m":"<h1>Post 1762820482988957839</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762820482988957839\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-28T12:42:09Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1762982571841864016":{"a":"<p>I think most people in this world don&#x27;t consider the consequences of their actions. What you do with the knowledge of your error is key.<br>\n<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RKwkM4uraRg\">YouTube</a></p>\n<p>Karma isn&#x27;t just some vague concept. It&#x27;s the reflections of moment of every day; every action has equal and opposite…</p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/RKwkM4uraRg\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\"></iframe><p class=\"embed-fallback\"><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RKwkM4uraRg\">Watch on YouTube</a></p></div>","m":"<h1>Post 1762982571841864016</h1>\n<p><a href=\"https://x.com/DavidLNorris/status/1762982571841864016\">View on X</a></p>\n<dl>\n<dt>when</dt><dd>2024-02-28T23:26:14Z</dd><dt>type</dt><dd>original</dd><dt>lang</dt><dd>en</dd><dt>likes</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>reposts</dt><dd>0</dd><dt>replies</dt><dd>0</dd>\n</dl>"},"1762990863192404222":{"a":"<p><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YJOlngk8D6E\">YouTube</a></p>\n<div class=\"embed embed-youtube\"><iframe src=\"https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/YJOlngk8D6E\" title=\"YouTube\" allowfullscreen referrerpolicy=\"strict-origin-when-